# Published volumes — the artifact `cartographer publish` writes, mounted at /out.
#
# Operator-local and large: a us-west volume measures 142.6 MB of JSON, and the photos are separate bytes
# again — 11.6 MB for the 182 published by the first bounded crawl, and on the order of 1 GB once the full
# 8,363-file crawl has run. `media/` is a sibling of the version directories and shared across them, so it
# outlives any one version. All of it is reproducible from the build database plus the signing key, so
# there is nothing here worth committing.
#
# The directory is tracked (this file only) so the bind mount finds it already owned by the host user.
# Docker would otherwise create it as root, and the container runs as `node` — see the note in
# docker-compose.yml.
*
!.gitignore
